## Context

Decision 0001 groups by normalized subject. The #4471 investigation finds distinct parser
and form-hint causes behind similar subjects. The supplied classifier and DedupeExplorer
already distinguish these causes using tenant locale, form version and report channel.

## Proposed decision

Read each report, deduplicate IDs, resolve its tenant, and compare the cause before merging.
Matching subjects are a search aid, not proof. Different subjects do not prevent a merge
when evidence establishes the same cause. Unknown tenants stay unresolved until investigated.
Keep one-day observations visible as uncertainty instead of inventing a confirmed cause.

## Consequences

Triage needs more context than a subject comparison, but engineering receives separate
fixes with auditable counts. The desk must approve this proposal before it supersedes
accepted decision 0001; that accepted record remains unchanged.

